<div class="oop-content-container">

    <div class="alert alert-danger" role="alert" style="margin-bottom: 2rem; border-left: 5px solid #dc3545; background: #fff5f5; padding: 1rem;">
        <h4 style="color: #dc3545; margin-top: 0;"><i class="fa-solid fa-lock"></i> Teacher Eyes Only</h4>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">Solutions for Level E: Logbook Aggregation.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Concept Overview</h2>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 1.5rem;">
            <li><strong>Aggregation</strong>: The Player <em>may have</em> a Logbook (it can exist independently), unlike Composition (Inventory) which dies with the player.</li>
            <li><strong>Dependency Injection</strong>: We create the Logbook outside and pass it in (`attach_logbook`).</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Common Misconceptions</h2>
        <div class="info-content">
            <p><strong>1. `self.logbook` initialization</strong></p>
            <p>It must start as `None` in `__init__`. We only set it when `attach_logbook` is called.</p>
            
            <p><strong>2. Defensive Programming</strong></p>
            <p>In `record_event`, students must check `if self.logbook is None`. If they don't, the game will crash if they try to log something before obtaining the device.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Solution Code</h2>
        
        <h3>logbook.py</h3>
        <div class="code-block" style="background: #1e1e1e; color: #d4d4d4; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 6px; overflow-x: auto; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
            <pre><code>class Logbook:
    def __init__(self):
        self._entries = []

    def add_entry(self, entry):
        self._entries.append(entry)

    def list_entries(self):
        return list(self._entries)  # Copy</code></pre>
        </div>
        
        <h3>player.py (additions)</h3>
        <div class="code-block" style="background: #1e1e1e; color: #d4d4d4; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 6px; overflow-x: auto;">
            <pre><code>    def attach_logbook(self, logbook):
        self.logbook = logbook

    def record_event(self, entry):
        if self.logbook is None:
            return "No logbook attached."
            
        self.logbook.add_entry(entry)
        return "Logbook updated."</code></pre>
        </div>
    </section>

